          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            is a context of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
            notion of
            %em cohesion
            on their collections of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean-topological+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} topological cohesion
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth cohesion
          %p
            While the axioms of cohesion do imply the intrinsic existence of
            %em exponentiated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+spaces"} infinitesimal spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic
            notion of infinitesimal extension.
          %p
            Here we consider one extra axiom on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            that does imply a good intrinsic notion of synthetic differential extension, compatible with the given notion of cohesion. We speak of
            = succeed "." do
              %em differential cohesion
          %p
            In a cohesive
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formal smoothness
            and of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+space"} de Rham space
          %h2#differential_cohesion Differential cohesion
          %p
            We discuss
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            that encodes a refinement of the corresponding notion of cohesion to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
              cohesion
            \. More precisely, we consider inclusions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{H}_{th}
            of cohesive
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-toposes that exhibit the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th}
            as infinitesimal cohesive neighbourhoods of objects in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %h3#Definition Definition
          #InfinitesimalCohesiveInfTopos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a cohesive
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
