          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This definition captures the characterization of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal object
              as having a single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global point
              surrounded by an infinitesimal neighbourhood: as we shall see in more detail
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalPathsAndReduction"} below
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*
              may be thought of as contracting away any infinitesimal extension of an object. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              being an
              %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalObject"} infinitesimal object
              amounts to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* X \simeq *
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_! \dashv i^*)
              then indeed guarantees that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
