            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              In traditional contexts see (
              %a{:href => "#SimpsonTeleman"}> SimpsonTeleman, p. 7
              ) the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im(X)
              is called the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+space"} de Rham space
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              or the
              %strong
                de Rham stack of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              \. Here we may tend to avoid this terminology, since by the discussion at
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos#deRhamCohomology"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos – de Rham cohomology
              we have a good notion of intrinsic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
              in any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              already without equipping it with differential cohesion. From this point of view the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im(X)
              is not primarily characterized by the fact that (in some models, see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#Examples"} below
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Π
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Pi}_{dR}(X)
              from
              %a{:href => "#deRhamCohomology"} above
              does, too – but by the fact that it does so in an explicitly (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"}> synthetic
              ) infinitesimal way.
          #InclusionOfConstantIntoInfinitesimalIntoAllPaths.num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              There is a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Im(X) \to \int(X)
            %p that factors the finite path inclusion through the infinitesimal one
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∫
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \Im(X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; \int(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              This is the formula for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              of the composite adjunction
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mi th
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Disc
                              %mi inf
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Π
                              %mi inf
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ←
                          %mi Disc
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi Π
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th} \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_{inf}}{\to}}{\underset{Disc_{inf}}{\leftarrow}} \mathbf{H} \stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\to}}{\underset{Disc}{\leftarrow}} \infty Grpd
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi inf
                        %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi Disc
                      %mi inf
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Disc
                          %mi inf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mi inf
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Disc
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi Disc
                      %mi inf
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi inf
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Disc
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mi th
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mi th
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{i_{inf}X}{\to} Disc_{inf}\Pi_{inf} X
                    \\stackrel{Disc_{inf}(i_{\mathbf{H}}\Pi_{inf}X)}{\to}
                    Disc_{\mathbf{H}} Disc_{inf} \Pi_{\mathbf{H}} \Pi_{inf} X
                    \=
                    Disc_{\mathbf{H}_{th}} \Pi_{\mathbf{H}_{th}}
                    \\,.
          %h5#JetBundleObjects
            Jet
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change+geometric+morphism"} base change geometric morphism
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} over-(∞,1)-toposes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f^* \dashv f_*) : \mathbf{H}/X \stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}} \mathbf{H}/Y
                  \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Jet
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi i
                            %mo *
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Jet : \mathbf{H}/X \stackrel{\overset{i^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{i_*}{\to}}
                    \\mathbf{H}/\Im(X)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change+geometric+morphism"} base change geometric morphism
              induced by the constant infinitesimal path inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : X \to \Im(X)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalPathsAndReduction"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E \to X) \in \mathbf{H}/X
              we call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Jet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Jet(E) \to \Im(X)
              as well as its pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi Jet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* Jet(E) \to X
              (depending on context) the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
          %h5#formally_smoothtaleunramified_morphisms Formally smooth/étale/unramified morphisms
          #FormalSmoothness.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              We say an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}_{th}
              is
              %strong formally smooth
              if the constant infinitesimal path inclusion,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \Im(X)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalPathsAndReduction"}
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
          %p
            In this form this is the evident
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SimpsonTeleman"} SimpsonTeleman, page 7
          #FormalSmoothnessByCanonicalMorphism.num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}_{th}
              is formally smooth according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothness"}
              precisely if the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_! X \to i_* X
            %p
              (induced from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_! \dashv i^* \dashv i_* \dashv i^!)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p The canonical morphism is the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                    %mi ℑ
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i_! \to i_*)
                    \:=
                    i_!
                    
                    \\stackrel{\eta i_!}{\to}
                    \\Im i_! := i_* i^* i_!
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    i_*
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
              the second morphism here in an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              being an effective epimorphism is equivalent to the component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Π
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_! X \to \mathbf{\Pi} i_! X
              being an effective epimorphism.
          #RelationToRK.num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              In this form this characterization of formal smoothness is the evident generalization of the condition given in (
              %a{:href => "#KontsevichRosenbergSpaces"}> Kontsevich-Rosenberg, section 4.1
              ). See the section
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Q-category#FormalSmoothness"} Formal smoothness
              at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Q-category"} Q-category
              for more discussion. Notice that by
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Q-category#DiscussionOfTheInfinitesimalThickeningFormalization"} this remark
              the notation there is related to the one used here by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^* = i_!
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_* = i^*
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mo !
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^! = i_*
          %p Therefore we have the following more general definition.
          #FormalRelativeSmoothnessByCanonicalMorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              a morphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth morphism
                  if the canonical morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                        %mi Y
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Y
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        i_! X
                        \\to
                        i_! Y \prod_{i_* Y} i_* Y
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+unramified+morphism"} formally unramified morphism
                  if this is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
                  morphism. More generally,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is an
                  %em
                    order-
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                    formally unramified morphisms
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-2) \leq k \leq \infty
                  if this is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-truncated"} k-truncated
                  morphism.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
                  if this morphism is an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo !
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mo !
                                    %mi f
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo !
                                %mi Y
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mo *
                                    %mi f
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                                %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        i_! X &amp;\stackrel{i_! f}{\to}&amp; i_! Y
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        i_* X &amp;\stackrel{i_* f}{\to}&amp; i_* Y
                        }
                %p
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
                  square.
          #MeaningOfFormallyUnramified.num_remark
            %h6#remark_9 Remark
            %p
              An order-(-2) formally unramified morphism is equivalently a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
            %p
              Only for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              does formal smoothness together with formal unramifiedness imply formal étaleness.
          %p
            Even more generally we can formulate formal smoothness in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th}
          #FormallyEtaleInHTh.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th}
              is
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+etale+morphism"} formally étale
              if it is
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℑ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pi-closed+morphism"} closed
              = succeed "-unit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℑ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \Im(X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im(f)}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\to&amp; \Im(y)
                    }
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is formally etale in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalRelativeSmoothnessByCanonicalMorphism"}
              precisely if its image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!(f)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th}
              is formally etale in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormallyEtaleInHTh"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              This is again given by the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im = i_* i^*
              by definition and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              is fully faithful, so that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo !
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %msup
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo !
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_! X &amp;\to&amp; \Im(i_! X) \simeq i_* i^* i_! X &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; i_* X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_! f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_* i^* i_! f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_* f}}
                    \\\
                    i_! Y &amp;\to&amp; \Im(i_! Y) \simeq i_* i^* i_! Y &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; i_* Y
                    }
                    \\,.
          #PropertiesOfFormallyEtaleMorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} formally étale morphisms
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalRelativeSmoothnessByCanonicalMorphism"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
                  is formally étale.
              %li
                %p The composite of two formally étale morphisms is itself formally étale.
              %li
                %p If
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi f
                                %mo ↗
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⇙
                                  %mo ≃
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi g
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi h
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; Y
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\nearrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                        \\\
                        X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{h}{\to}&amp;&amp; Z
                        }
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
                  are formally étale, then also
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is formally étale.
              %li
                %p
                  Any
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                  of a formally étale morphisms is itself formally étale.
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
                  of a formally étale morphisms is formally étale if the pullback is preserved by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
          %p
            The statements about closure under composition and pullback appears as(
            %a{:href => "#KontsevichRosenbergSpaces"}> KontsevichRosenberg, prop. 5.4, prop. 5.6
            ). Notice that the extra assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
            preserves the pullback is implicit in their setup, by remark
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationToRK"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              The first statement follows since
              = succeed "-pullbacks" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %p
              The second two statements follow by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              for
              = succeed "s:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : Y \to Z
              be two morphisms and consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo !
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo !
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Z
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo *
                                %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_! X &amp;\stackrel{i_! f }{\to}&amp; i_! Y &amp;\stackrel{i_! g}{\to}&amp;  Z
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    i_* X &amp;\stackrel{i_* f }{\to}&amp; i_* Y &amp;\stackrel{i_* g}{\to}&amp; i_* Z
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are formally étale then both small squares are pullback squares. Then the pasting law says that so is the outer rectangle and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
              is formally étale. Similarly, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \circ f
              are formally étale then the right square and the total reactangle are pullbacks, so the pasting law says that also the left square is a pullback and so also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is formally étale.
            %p
              For the fourth claim, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Id
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id \simeq (g \to f \to g)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow (∞,1)-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : i_! \to I_*
              we obtain a retract
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Id
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi g
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mi g
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Id \simeq ((i_! g \to i_*g) \to  (i_! f \to i_*f) \to (i_! g \to i_*g))
            %p
              in the category of squares
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mo □
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^{\Box}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo □
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^\Box
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              square, then so is its retract sqare. This implies the fourth claim.
            %p To see this, we use that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"}> (∞,1)-limit
                  s are computed by
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  presenting
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %li
                %p
                  homotopy limits in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  may be computed by the left and right adjoints provided by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivator"} derivator
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C)
                  associated to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              From this the claim follows as described in detail at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              in the section
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/retract#RetractsOfDiagrams"} retracts of diagrams
              \.
            %p
              For the last claim, consider an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi Y
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A \times_Y X &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is formally étale.
            %p
              Applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : i_! \to i_*
              to this yields a square of squares. Two sides of this are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi Y
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo !
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo !
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_! A \times_Y X &amp;\to&amp; i_! X &amp;\stackrel{\phi_X}{\to}&amp;  i_* X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_! p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_! f}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_* f}}
                    \\\
                    i_! A &amp;\to&amp; i_! Y &amp;\stackrel{\phi_Y}{\to}&amp; i_* Y
                    }
            %p and the other two sides are the pasting composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi Y
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi A
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ×
                                      %mi Y
                                    %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi Y
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo !
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi p
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    i_! A \times_Y X &amp;\stackrel{\phi_{A \times_Y X}}{\to}&amp; i_* A \times_Y A
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; i_* X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_! p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_* p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_* f}}
                    \\\
                    i_! A &amp;\stackrel{\phi_A}{\to}&amp; i_* A &amp;\to&amp; i_* Y
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Counting left to right and top to bottom, we have that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the first square is a pullback by assumption that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
                  preserves the given pullback;
              %li
                %p
                  the second square is a pullback, since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is formally étale.
              %li
                %p
                  the total top rectangle is therefore a pullback, by the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %li
                %p
                  the fourth square is a pullback since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_*
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  and so also preserves pullbacks;
              %li
                %p also the total bottom rectangle is a pullback, since it is equal to the top total rectangle;
              %li
                %p
                  therefore finally the third square is a pullback, by the other clause of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is formally étale.
          #AsOpenMaps.num_remark
            %h6#remark_11 Remark
            %p
              The properties listed in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropertiesOfFormallyEtaleMorphisms"}
              correspond to the axioms on the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"}> open map
                s
              (“admissible maps”) in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometry (for structured (∞,1)-toposes)
              (
              %a{:href => "#LurieStSp"}> Lurie, def. 1.2.1
              ). This means that a notion of formally étale morphisms induces a notion of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+algebra-ed+topos"} locally algebra-ed (∞,1)toposes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} structured (∞,1)-toposes
              in a cohesive context. This is discuss in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+--+structure+%E2%88%9E-sheaves"}> cohesive (∞,1)-topos – structure ∞-sheaves
                \.
          %p In order to interpret the notion of formal smoothness, we turn now to the discussion of infinitesimal reduction.
          #RedIsIdempotent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
              projection of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{th}
              onto the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Re \Re \simeq \Re
                    \\,.
            %p Accordingly also
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Im \Im \simeq \Im
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              By definition of infinitesimal neighbourhood we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* i_! \simeq Id
              and hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℜ
                            %mi ℜ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo !
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi ℜ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Re \Re
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    i_! i^* i_! i^*
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq i_! i^*
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq \Re
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          #PiInfXIsFormallySmooth.num_cor
            %h6#observation_2 Observation
            %p
              For every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mi th
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}_{th}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im(X)
              is formally smooth according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormalSmoothness"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RedIsIdempotent"}
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Im(X) \to \Im \Im X
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
          %h4#InfinitesimalA1Homotopy
            Infinitesimal
            = succeed "-homotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p
              A set of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi th
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi α
